  Slug: silence-in-snow
  DisplayName: Silence in Snow
  IconPath: icons/magic/water/bubbles-air-water-light.webp
  Description: "Bitter cold heralded your patron's appearance, in the depths of the
    winter solstice or on a frozen peak at the end of the world. Your patron might
    be a winter hag, ice yai, or other spirit of the cold, but one thing is clear
    as ice\u2014their power is not to be underestimated. Spell List primal Patron
    Skill Nature Lesson of Winter's Chill Your patron taught you the power of winter
    firsthand by subjecting you to frost and snow. You learn the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Clinging
    Ice] hex cantrip and your familiar learns @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Gust
    of Wind]. Familiar of Freezing Rime Your familiar is cold to the touch, its breath
    always visible. When you Cast or Sustain a hex, you can cause ice to form in
    a @Template[burst|distance:5] centered on a square of your familiar's space.
    Those squares are difficult terrain until the start of your next turn."
